Rollout patch 0008: the explicit-fma campaign (PORTING 14 backlog item 1).

The build compiles -ffp-contract=off for bit-parity (7); that also costs every
kernel its fused multiply-adds - nvcc contracts a*b+c for free and we do not.
This patch introduces EXPLICIT __fmaf_rn at the hot per-token sites so the
fused instruction is emitted regardless of the flag, with every touched kernel
gated by its existing parity test (bound/tolerance gates are fusion-tolerant
by construction; the one bit-pinned test flips its reference to the fused
model in the same patch, keeping its fused!=unfused sensitivity check).

Sites: s2_gemv_q8 (4, the engine S2 path), bf16_gemv (3 kernels x their MAC),
native_rope (the + rotation form; a*c - b*s has no fma form and stays),
native_gdn (kv shard dot, rank-1 update, readout), gdn canonical (both 128-iter
passes + 4-tap conv; fp64 norm loops stay unfused - RDNA3 fp64 fma is not a
win), native_flash_attn (QK dot x2, softmax rescale), native_mmvq epilogues
(q5_k/q4_k dual chains, q2_0/q6_k chains; dp4a bodies are integer-immune),
elementwise embedding_gather (+ its parity reference flip).

Semantics: __fmaf_rn(a, b, 0) == the rn multiply, so no-offset paths are
bit-identical; everywhere else the result is the CORRECTLY-ROUNDED product-sum
where the old code double-rounded - a tighter arithmetic, not a looser one.

